  "implementation_review": [
    "Common all-declaration checking and cycle/access/effect/owner checks run before Meaning validation. The callback uses original borrowed Index identities; no reconstructed AST or span/name lookup.",
    "The shared finite interpreter evaluates exact ordinary expressions and eagerly evaluates call arguments in source order. Callee patterns use their own resolved BinderIds and unchanged original bodies.",
    "Unit, Bit, Bits and every product constructor remain distinct Type<u32> nodes; widths only label finite inputs, never identify exact source types. Zero-width Unit factors occupy their original product positions.",
    "A permutation target enumerates every original classical function input and reports duplicate outputs with both inputs. Exact phase targets retain the three-Bit product, including Unit scalar values.",
    "Existing limits remain: 6-bit target dimension, 12-bit ordinary expression width, depth64,4096 type nodes and common1000000 work. Table/collision cells, type copies, binders, fields and phase signature nodes are charged before allocation/copy. These are preparation capacities, not quantitative RS evidence.",
    "Nested expression errors retain the actual source module. Collision diagnostics locate the original Meaning declaration.",
    "Meaning-refined parameters and checked_op concrete projection guards remain. A generated/validated finite table grants neither provider equality nor native execution. Provider substitution, independent target requests and actual output binding remain unfinished.",
    "No Lean/schema/primitive/accepted-handle/effect/guarantee/dependency/version changes."
  ],
  "new_conformance_tests": [
    "selected_preparation_rejects_unused_nonpermutation_meanings",
    "selected_meaning_checks_follow_original_imports_and_forward_calls",
    "selected_meaning_preparation_keeps_zero_width_and_product_type_tags",
    "selected_meaning_preparation_handles_scalar_phase_and_pattern_leaf_order"
  ],
